30:14.750 --> 30:16.582
What?
Oh, thank you. No.

30:16.583 --> 30:17.915
No. He is a fireman.

30:17.916 --> 30:19.790
Firefighter, we say.
Firefighter.

30:19.791 --> 30:21.165
You're a firefighter?

30:21.166 --> 30:23.332
You're not a...
You weren't a firefighter.

30:23.333 --> 30:25.040
Yeah, he was a fire captain.

30:25.041 --> 30:27.082
- You were a fire captain?
- Captain Hawk?

30:27.083 --> 30:29.249
- Captain Hawk. No, you weren't.
- Oh, my God.

30:29.250 --> 30:31.540
You're not Captain Hawk.
That's bullshit.

30:31.541 --> 30:33.207
- Why?
- "Why"?

30:33.208 --> 30:34.707
You don't seem like
a firefighter.

30:34.708 --> 30:36.415
What does a firefighter
seem like?

30:36.416 --> 30:38.082
They're brawnier.
They're brawnier.

30:38.083 --> 30:39.790
- They have moustaches.
- What do you mean?

30:39.791 --> 30:42.290
- They're brawnier
- ¿Qué es eso de "brawny"?

30:42.291 --> 30:44.415
- Fuerte. Fuerte.
- More fuerte. More fuerte.

30:44.416 --> 30:45.999
He's very fuerte.

30:46.000 --> 30:48.207
He's pretty fuerte, although
he could be more fuerte.

30:48.208 --> 30:50.040
I don't know
if he's fireman fuerte.

30:50.041 --> 30:51.332
I was more fuerte
in the beginning,

30:51.333 --> 30:53.457
but I was, you know...

30:53.458 --> 30:56.832
I got to my pension.
I just decided I'd had enough

30:56.833 --> 31:01.499
and kind of gave up my hose
for the command job, and then...

31:01.500 --> 31:03.207
- Thank God.
- ...I retired

31:03.208 --> 31:05.915
and just started pursuing
my other interests

31:05.916 --> 31:08.915
- and new adventures.
- Now he's studying roofing.

31:08.916 --> 31:11.040
- Roofing. Beautiful.
- The adventure of roofing.

31:11.041 --> 31:14.374
- No, sorry. Rolfing. Rolfing.
- That's what I said.

31:14.375 --> 31:16.082
- Rolfing.
- Rolfing.

31:16.083 --> 31:17.457
- Say it again.
- No.

31:17.458 --> 31:19.291
Say it again.

31:22.291 --> 31:25.040
You're a masseuse now.
That's cool.

31:25.041 --> 31:26.415
You gonna work
in the Four Seasons?

31:26.416 --> 31:28.665
No, no. Rolfing's a...

31:28.666 --> 31:31.165
It's a much deeper modality.

31:31.166 --> 31:35.457
It... It... It's challenging
for both parties, really.

31:35.458 --> 31:37.749
But, um... yeah, to be healing.

31:37.750 --> 31:40.832
I'm almost certified.
You wanna jump on my table, Joe?

31:40.833 --> 31:43.250
Never in a million years.

31:45.458 --> 31:47.958
Yeah...
I really love you, Joe.

31:49.125 --> 31:50.541
What do you love about me, Hawk?

31:52.625 --> 31:55.291
I like how honest you are
about what you're feeling.

31:56.500 --> 31:59.249
Well,
in the pursuit of honesty...

31:59.250 --> 32:00.874
Who wants a house tour?

32:00.875 --> 32:02.749
Would you like to see more?
There's so much more.

32:02.750 --> 32:04.207
- I do.
- Great.

32:04.208 --> 32:05.832
- Yeah. I definitely do.
- Yeah.

32:05.833 --> 32:08.540
I'm actually gonna smoke
a joint. I've seen the place.

32:08.541 --> 32:10.874
What? Now?
Joe! No!

32:10.875 --> 32:13.249
Can I come with you?

32:13.250 --> 32:15.499
- Really?
- Yeah. Can I?

32:15.500 --> 32:19.457
- Sure. Totally.
- You gonna go up to the roof?

32:19.458 --> 32:22.582
I thought I'd just, you know,
maybe go in my office.

32:22.583 --> 32:24.540
That's cool, right? Unless
you have a problem with that.

32:24.541 --> 32:26.290
- No. Yeah. Yeah.
- Cool. Right?

32:26.291 --> 32:28.832
- Cool. Yeah. Cool. Yeah.
- So, yeah. Yeah. Cool, right?

32:28.833 --> 32:31.207
- Cool. Yeah. Let's go.
- Uh...

32:31.208 --> 32:33.749
Do you wanna open a window
'cause... you know.

32:33.750 --> 32:35.250
- Yeah, sure.
- Great.

32:39.500 --> 32:41.124
A lot of stuff in here.

32:41.125 --> 32:43.874
What do you got
other than this?

32:43.875 --> 32:45.457
- You saw this.
- Copenhagen Designs.

32:45.458 --> 32:47.207
Oh, if you like...
Let's... Here.

32:47.208 --> 32:49.832
We'll start in here.
I wanna show you...

32:49.833 --> 32:53.374
- You spend a lot of time here.
- I do. You can tell?

32:53.375 --> 32:55.957
- Yes, I can.
- Yeah, it's...

32:55.958 --> 32:57.624
It's a little messy.
I'm usually...

32:57.625 --> 32:59.916
um, you know,
usually alone in here.

33:05.250 --> 33:07.166
There you go.

33:08.125 --> 33:09.749
There you go.

33:09.750 --> 33:11.415
But chaos...

33:11.416 --> 33:13.249
Biggest sign of creativity.

33:13.250 --> 33:14.999
Really? Good. Great.

33:15.000 --> 33:17.582
It means you're focused
on more important things.

33:17.583 --> 33:19.582
Oh, you know, that's...

33:19.583 --> 33:21.832
That's how I like
to think of it. Not sure...

33:21.833 --> 33:23.957
Not sure Angela would
agree with that.

33:23.958 --> 33:27.290
She purges things.
Disgusting in here.

33:27.291 --> 33:30.457
I actually did
all of this grouting myself,

33:30.458 --> 33:32.790
which I love.
I... I find it meditative.

33:32.791 --> 33:34.540
Joe thinks I'm insane.

33:34.541 --> 33:36.957
And then the floor... I mean,
I'm sure this is something

33:36.958 --> 33:38.707
- you might have picked up.
- No.

33:38.708 --> 33:40.207
No?

33:40.208 --> 33:43.499
- Original ceramic penny tile.
- Wow.

33:43.500 --> 33:44.874
Anyway, that was

33:44.875 --> 33:46.499
sort of similar
to what was there before.

33:46.500 --> 33:48.665
But that was kind of
what I was going for with the...

33:48.666 --> 33:51.665
The whole theme was, um...
renovation without change,

33:51.666 --> 33:55.165
which I think I succeeded in,

33:55.166 --> 33:56.957
you know,
just to keep it original,

33:56.958 --> 33:59.874
but with a new surface.

33:59.875 --> 34:04.457
I mean, admittedly,
I know a lot less about tile

34:04.458 --> 34:06.374
than I've learned about rugs,

34:06.375 --> 34:08.999
and a lot of the bathrooms
that I've seen

34:09.000 --> 34:11.457
- have been on fire, so, my...
- Oh, no.

34:11.458 --> 34:13.165
...my relationship with them
was fleeting.

34:13.166 --> 34:14.915
But, um, I'd have just said

34:14.916 --> 34:18.083
this was an immaculately
preserved vintage...

34:19.791 --> 34:21.249
...bathroom.

34:21.250 --> 34:24.540
Wow. Um, that's
what I was going for. That's...

34:24.541 --> 34:26.874
- You fooled me.
- Wow!

34:26.875 --> 34:30.165
- Oh! Facebook marketplace.
- Come on.

34:30.166 --> 34:32.124
The jamón is not...
is not jamón.

34:32.125 --> 34:34.499
- That's not jamón?
- No, it's really prosciutto.

34:34.500 --> 34:36.207
- It's prosciutto?
- Which is OK.

34:36.208 --> 34:37.832
It doesn't look like jamón.
It looks like prosciutto.

34:37.833 --> 34:39.374
But I didn't wanna
say anything.

34:39.375 --> 34:40.582
No, yeah, don't.

34:40.583 --> 34:42.207
If you told her
that wasn't jamón,

34:42.208 --> 34:44.540
she would commit suicide
in our dining room.

34:44.541 --> 34:46.040
I'm telling you that right now.

34:46.041 --> 34:48.582
She can't take it.
She could not take that.

34:48.583 --> 34:50.208
More?

34:51.750 --> 34:54.082
- You good?
- No, no.

34:54.083 --> 34:57.415
Like, I... I don't want more
because then...

34:57.416 --> 34:59.415
If I have more than one hit,

34:59.416 --> 35:02.207
I start counting objects,
and I can't stop,

35:02.208 --> 35:04.290
and imagine what that
would be like in here.

35:04.291 --> 35:06.290
You start counting
objects?

35:06.291 --> 35:07.999
I've never heard of that.

35:08.000 --> 35:10.707
We'd lose you for the rest
of your life.

35:10.708 --> 35:14.749
Exactly. What is this?

35:14.750 --> 35:16.749
It's...
It's for a xylophone.

35:16.750 --> 35:18.790
Exactly.
You figured it out.

35:18.791 --> 35:20.874
It's intuitive, ultimately.

35:20.875 --> 35:23.124
There's only one of those,
so you're OK.

35:23.125 --> 35:25.499
Figured it out.

35:25.500 --> 35:27.749
This is actually, um...

35:27.750 --> 35:32.582
This is where the two
apartments were combined.

35:32.583 --> 35:35.415
And you can just see the...
'cause it's a bit thicker there,

35:35.416 --> 35:37.999
that that's where they, um...

35:38.000 --> 35:40.999
where there used to be
a separation.

35:41.000 --> 35:43.165
- A wall.
- Wall!

35:43.166 --> 35:45.415
That was...
what they call a wall.

35:45.416 --> 35:47.207
The technical term is "wall".

35:47.208 --> 35:49.124
We literally
are just that much, so...

35:49.125 --> 35:50.415
Oh, right,
'cause you guys are...

35:50.416 --> 35:52.749
- Yeah, yeah. It's so lucky.
- Huh!

35:52.750 --> 35:55.790
Well, so, this is Maggie's room,
and I actually did...

35:55.791 --> 35:57.249
I did all the stenciling,

35:57.250 --> 35:59.040
and she's probably
a little old for it now.

35:59.041 --> 36:00.665
I'm probably gonna
have to change it, but I...

36:00.666 --> 36:03.999
- No, it's cute.
- Yeah, it's... Yeah.

36:04.000 --> 36:06.207
The carpeting is...

36:06.208 --> 36:08.124
- Oh!
- Wow.

36:08.125 --> 36:10.415
- Oh.
- God. That's so good.

36:10.416 --> 36:13.457
- Oh!
- Is that, like, Larry Salton?

36:13.458 --> 36:15.958
Oh, no. No. No, no.
That... That is me.

36:17.583 --> 36:20.707
- You took it?
- Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

36:20.708 --> 36:23.082
Wow! Do you work
as a photographer?

36:23.083 --> 36:24.749
No.

36:24.750 --> 36:27.165
No, I went to art school,
like, a million years ago,

36:27.166 --> 36:29.749
and I got a degree
I did literally nothing with,

36:29.750 --> 36:31.582
and that is from then.

36:31.583 --> 36:34.832
I mean, I think...
you know, you...

36:34.833 --> 36:36.957
Your creativity
is all over this place.

36:36.958 --> 36:38.791
I think you're really talented.

36:40.208 --> 36:41.749
Thank you.

36:41.750 --> 36:43.540
What about this?

36:43.541 --> 36:46.582
Oh, that's, no, 'cause that...
That's the bedroom, which is...

36:46.583 --> 36:48.374
- What's going on in here?
- Yeah.

36:48.375 --> 36:50.249
No, I know, I didn't...
I didn't...

36:50.250 --> 36:53.082
It's... not part of the tour.

36:53.083 --> 36:56.499
- It's a pretty important room.
- Yeah... Yeah.

36:56.500 --> 36:57.915
Yes. He is a fireman.

36:57.916 --> 36:59.790
He's really
a fireman? Yeah.

36:59.791 --> 37:02.207
How long
have you been with him?

37:02.208 --> 37:05.332
Uh... one year.
A little less than one year.

37:05.333 --> 37:06.957
- One year. That's it?
- Mm.

37:06.958 --> 37:08.374
Oh, wow.

37:08.375 --> 37:10.083
Would've thought longer.

37:12.000 --> 37:14.207
I was married before.

37:14.208 --> 37:16.040
- Really?
- Yeah.

37:16.041 --> 37:17.249
Interesting.

37:17.250 --> 37:20.207
How did you meet the fireman?

37:20.208 --> 37:22.499
He was my patient.

37:22.500 --> 37:24.165
He was your patient?

37:24.166 --> 37:26.832
And then you started dating him?

37:26.833 --> 37:28.290
Piña!

37:28.291 --> 37:31.832
This was Joe's parents' house.

37:31.833 --> 37:33.207
- Oh, wow.
- Yeah.

37:33.208 --> 37:34.915
- He grew up here?
- He grew up here.

37:34.916 --> 37:38.915
Yeah. He was conceived
right here.

37:38.916 --> 37:40.540
- On this bed?
- No. No, no, different bed.

37:40.541 --> 37:42.665
- Oh, good. Yeah.
- Different mattress.

37:42.666 --> 37:44.790
- Different bed.
- Parental fluids is, like,

37:44.791 --> 37:46.499
a little bit too intimate, maybe.

37:46.500 --> 37:49.040
I mean, he hates...
hates people knowing this,

37:49.041 --> 37:50.749
- so don't...
- Why?

37:50.750 --> 37:53.124
Because, I mean, we could
never in a million years

37:53.125 --> 37:55.332
afford this place.

37:55.333 --> 37:58.374
No shame in that. Like, nobody
in America can afford anything.

37:58.375 --> 38:00.749
Yeah, but he just...
He really...

38:00.750 --> 38:02.499
- It's a bit... eezzz!
- That's crazy.

38:02.500 --> 38:05.165
- Yeah, it's not a...
- It's such a gift. I mean...

38:05.166 --> 38:07.707
- Just...
- Well, that's what I think.

38:07.708 --> 38:11.082
- Make it positive, you know?
- Yeah.

38:11.083 --> 38:15.332
Be grateful and lean into it.
Make it your own, you know?

38:15.333 --> 38:17.290
- Yeah.
- So much pleasure in that.

38:17.291 --> 38:18.749
Yeah...

38:18.750 --> 38:20.166
Yeah.

38:24.250 --> 38:25.999
Can I ask you something?

38:26.000 --> 38:27.790
Sure.

38:27.791 --> 38:29.790
I just... I have a...

38:29.791 --> 38:31.832
I have a decision to make,
and I...

38:31.833 --> 38:34.374
I feel like you might be able
to help me make it.

38:34.375 --> 38:37.707
I mean, if I can, yeah.

38:37.708 --> 38:39.290
Wait, did you
leave your husband for Hawk?

38:39.291 --> 38:41.957
- Is that what happened?
- No, no, no. I didn't.

38:41.958 --> 38:45.291
That relationship was over
when I met him.

38:49.875 --> 38:53.249
How did you know
that, uh... it was over,

38:53.250 --> 38:55.249
if you don't mind me asking?

38:55.250 --> 38:58.499
'Cause we stopped having sex,
then we stopped talking.

38:58.500 --> 39:01.957
Then we were strangers.

39:01.958 --> 39:05.999
People... people forget
that they deserve more.

39:06.000 --> 39:09.333
You know?
They start living on migajas.

39:10.291 --> 39:13.040
- Crumbs.
- Crumbs. Yeah.

39:13.041 --> 39:15.874
And I cannot live like that.
I'd rather die.

39:15.875 --> 39:19.374
I think you really
just have to listen to

39:19.375 --> 39:21.582
what is your heart
kind of pulling you toward,

39:21.583 --> 39:23.708
what vision of yourself?

39:24.916 --> 39:26.499
You know?

39:26.500 --> 39:29.374
I mean, do you see yourself
walking on a cold beach

39:29.375 --> 39:32.832
alone with the wind in your face
and the clarity of that?

39:32.833 --> 39:37.749
Or sitting on a southern porch
in the heat,

39:37.750 --> 39:40.250
holding hands and getting old...

39:42.875 --> 39:45.707
...or...

39:45.708 --> 39:49.125
...sitting in a Copenhagen café
with a stranger?

39:50.416 --> 39:53.082
I'd go with Copenhagen.

39:53.083 --> 39:54.957
